        <h2 id="e"><span class="num">2</span>How it is tested</h2>
        <p>The model is trained on data to 2016, and every design choice was frozen in September 2024. At each decision it sees sixty days and states the risk of the next twenty for nine long-only books, against five desk standards, six scalar forecasters and six generative families given the same information. Decisions before the freeze were used to choose the configuration; decisions after it were used for nothing but scoring.</p>
        <figure>
          <img src="/projects/diffusion-scenarios/media/stated-vs-realised.png" alt="Stated versus realised twenty-day volatility of the equal-weight book across three windows, with per-decision error gaps" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption><b>Figure 3.</b> The statement against what actually happened, on the equal-weight book: realised twenty-day volatility in black, the engine's statement in blue and filtered historical simulation in gold. Both miss the March 2020 jump; what separates them is the recovery after it. Figure from the manuscript.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2 id="r"><span class="num">3</span>What it shows</h2>
        <div class="take">
          <div><h4>What held up</h4><ul><li>One frozen checkpoint ran a standing risk process across 139 decisions and nine books, re-conditioned each morning and never refitted.</li><li>Before the freeze its book-risk error is below every desk standard; after it, the engine stays lowest in point estimate.</li><li>The advantage sits where the observed window is already volatile, at thresholds fixed before the confirmatory decisions were seen.</li><li>Unseen names and much wider universes cost a sampling pass, not a retraining.</li></ul></div>
          <div><h4>Where it stops</h4><ul><li>After the freeze the margins are not statistically resolved.</li><li>It does not state a jump on the day it happens; what separates it from a reactive estimator is the recovery.</li><li>The generated paths under-build volatility clustering and excess kurtosis.</li><li>It is a daily tool: on five-minute bars filtered historical simulation is the closer statement.</li></ul></div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="s"><span class="num">4</span>Status</h2>
        <p>Under review at Expert Systems with Applications since 2026.09.22. Code, checkpoints and a preprint will be released after the editorial decision. Next on this line: the shape defect the paths under-build, and phase-aware scenario generation with <a href="/research/finphasor/">FinPhasor</a>.</p>
